From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PM / devfreq: px30: pass the DRAM settings to BL31

BL31 takes the DRAM termination, drive strength and de-skew for each rate from the second shared page. Left empty it keeps the loader's 333 MHz setup, which corrupts memory at 666 MHz on some boards, so fill it with Rockchip's PX30 defaults.

--- a/drivers/devfreq/px30_dmc.c
+++ b/drivers/devfreq/px30_dmc.c
@@ -43,6 +43,154 @@
 	u32 complt_hwirq;
 };
 
